    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field following the codebase's established per-derivation helper pattern (`Locality`, `Timezone`, `ContactPreference`, \u2026), which keeps structural impact minimal.\n\n**Files touched (3):**\n\n1. **`OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 a small cohesive helper with one static method and no surrounding complexity:\n   ```java\n   public static String of(int membershipLevel, String locality) {\n       String tier = membershipLevel >= 3 ? \"PREMIUM\" : \"STANDARD\";\n       String area = METRO_REGIONS.contains(locality) ? \"METRO\" : \"REGIONAL\";\n       return tier + \"_\" + area;\n   }\n   ```\n   TIER from `membershipLevel >= 3`; AREA from locality \u2208 {NSW, VIC, QLD}.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` read-only string schema field so the generated `OwnerDto` gets its getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line wiring `ownerSegment` from the same subexpressions the existing `membershipLevel` and `locality` mappings already use.\n\nI avoided growing any existing method or class: the logic lives entirely in the new helper, and the mapper interface method only gained a single annotation. `STANDARD_METRO` (Sydney/NSW) and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` (unknown city) both verify against the new acceptance tests.",
